WEBVTT

0
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.380
There could be malware lurking right underneath your fingertips.

1
00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.329
Just by breaking down the word malware you can assume its meaning.

2
00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:11.489
The Latin root word mal,

3
00:00:11.649 --> 00:00:12.840
meaning bad or evil,

4
00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:15.470
like malicious malfunction and even dismal,

5
00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:16.420
plusware,

6
00:00:16.569 --> 00:00:18.170
referring to computer software,

7
00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:20.709
equates to bad software.

8
00:00:21.209 --> 00:00:24.549
Malware is any program or file harmful to a user.

9
00:00:24.969 --> 00:00:27.850
Types of malware include viruses which work on

10
00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:30.280
their own and spread to other programs,

11
00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:33.669
worms which self-replicate and spread autonomously.

12
00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:35.310
Trojan horses,

13
00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.799
which are disguised as legitimate programs to gain access to a system,

14
00:00:38.959 --> 00:00:39.740
spyware,

15
00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:42.700
which discreetly collects user information and activity,

16
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:44.180
ransomware,

17
00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.779
which encrypts a user's data and demands payment,

18
00:00:47.319 --> 00:00:48.720
and others like rootkits,

19
00:00:48.799 --> 00:00:49.319
adware,

20
00:00:49.439 --> 00:00:50.360
backdoor viruses,

21
00:00:50.479 --> 00:00:51.470
and key loggers.

22
00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:53.880
Malware authors usually want to steal financial,

23
00:00:54.009 --> 00:00:54.439
personal,

24
00:00:54.479 --> 00:00:55.860
or corporate information

25
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.919
to target advertisements or to control the device completely within a botnet.

26
00:01:00.689 --> 00:01:02.709
Some malware can be easily detected

27
00:01:02.849 --> 00:01:06.589
either by observing unusual activity or with antivirus software,

28
00:01:06.889 --> 00:01:08.349
and some can be removed.

29
00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:13.410
Having a malware response plan in place is key to lowering the chances of an attack

30
00:01:13.569 --> 00:01:15.410
and key to recovering from one.

31
00:01:15.769 --> 00:01:17.239
Have you had any malware run-ins?

32
00:01:17.569 --> 00:01:20.389
Share your experience in the comments and please hit that like button.